From 3546841bb1dc849f96bf1f622b2218aa75b235dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:30:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] NHFLOW: river free-surface initialisation (F 65), shared
 with SFLOW (river_ini)

The 1D river solver of F 65 moves from sflow_f_ini_river.cpp into the
class river_ini (river_ini.h/.cpp), used by SFLOW and NHFLOW:
start() gathers the global cross-sections and solves for the column
levels, eta() and velocity() give the values of a cell.

NHFLOW:
- F 65 1/2 set eta in nhflow_f::ini (after eta = 0, before WL and the
  wet flags); without F 60 the reference level wd is F 62
  (driver_logic_nhflow)
- F 65 2 sets U,V (and UH,VH = WL U, WL V; W = 0) on all layers of the
  wet cells after the potential-flow ini (driver_ini_nhflow), the strip
  velocity of the column friction slope along the i-direction
- friction law of the 1D solve: the log law at the centre of the
  bottom layer as nhflow_bcmom (A 519 1), u+ = 2.5 ln(30 z0/ks),
  z0 = dz0 h/2 (dz0 the sigma height of the bottom layer), with a
  depth-uniform velocity; SFLOW keeps Manning n = ks^(1/6)/20
- dry: WL below A 544 (SFLOW: A 244)

SFLOW results unchanged (river_ini law 0 is the code of before).

